CONCLUSION
Simulator adaptation measured by EDA is in its beginning. Our results suggest that a 35 minutes long drive gives enough time for participants exposed to a simulator for the first time to adapt. However, there is a tradeoff to make, as this makes the experiment less comfortable. We suggest that other researchers reproduce this study with less redundant circuits to see the impact of the trajectory itself. In addition, the number of participants of our study being small, further research is necessary to determine if the MSSQ can be used as a discriminator in the recruitment phase.
